{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event is a value conforming to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker"},{"text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SourceLocation"},{"text":" and its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"text":", as one of the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch(strategy:)"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:)"},{"text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"text":" for the consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"droppingCallSite()"},{"text":". A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentCategory"},{"text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"text":" value, which satisfies its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Constraint"},{"text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rejectionReports"},{"text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"); a control’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreensAutomatically"},{"text":", which tracks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"text":", which tracks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ControlActivated"},{"text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). On every platform, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackLifecycle"},{"text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). A tracker given the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions"},{"text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionEnded"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionStarted"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). A tracker given ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler"},{"text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SamplingDropReport"},{"text":" and stamping each kept record with its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRateKey"},{"text":". The standard enrichers, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.application()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operatingSystem()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendorIdentifier()"},{"text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" imports every module but ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","type":"reference"},{"text":", a product of its own for apps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that already use GRDB; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"reference"},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" macro derives an event’s conformances","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","type":"reference"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","type":"reference"},{"text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Tr